<title>CANADA: CAW, CAI, transport minister meet.</title>
<headline>CAW, CAI, transport minister meet.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Transport Minister David Anderson, Canadian Airlines Corp chief executive Kevin Benson and Canadian Auto Workers union president Buzz Hargrove began a meeting on Wednesday to discuss the fate of cash-strapped Canadian Airlines.</p>
<p>The CAW, representing about 3,700 of Canadian's 16,400 employees, is the only union that has refused to endorse Canadian's restructuring plan, calling instead for a government bailout for the airline.</p>
</text>
